@startuml fleet_monitor_singleton_port
'
' Plan 3 — Per-job monitor → singleton scanner port
'
' Shows the AFTER state: each fleet has ONE singleton monitor thread
' that scans all active jobs every 30s.  Replaces N per-job threads
' (one per active render) with 3 fleet-level singletons.
'
' Memory math: 50 active Vast + 50 active Modal jobs go from
' ~1010 MB long-lived thread overhead to ~35 MB.  Constant in active
' job count.

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false

title Plan 3 — Per-job monitor → singleton scanner port

package "fleets/vast" #FFE4FF {
  class VastFleetStrategy {
    + dispatch()
    + cancel(provider_job_id)
  }
  class VastFleetMonitor <<NEW, singleton>> {
    + try_start()
    - _loop()
    - _tick()
    - _inspect(row, inst)
  }
  class VastClient {
    + destroy(instance_id)
    + list()
  }

  VastFleetMonitor --> VastClient
}

note bottom of VastFleetMonitor
  Per-tick scan (every 30s):
   1. SELECT active Vast rows from PG (1 query)
   2. vast_client.list() — 1 API call, fleet-wide
   3. for row: _inspect(row, fleet[row.id])
  _inspect ports VastInstanceMonitor._tick
  decision blocks verbatim.
end note

note bottom of VastClient
  list() is the new bulk endpoint:
  GET /instances/?owner=me
  Returns every instance on the account.
end note

package "fleets/modal" #FFE4FF {
  class ModalFleetStrategy
  class ModalFleetMonitor <<NEW, singleton>> {
    + try_start()
    - _loop()
    - _tick()
    - _inspect(row)
  }

  ModalFleetStrategy --> ModalFleetMonitor
}

note bottom of ModalFleetMonitor
  No Modal API call per tick.
  Modal's per-job tick already reads only PG + Redis.
  SDK cancel only fires on terminal events.
end note

package "fleets/community" #DDFFDD {
  class CommunityMonitor <<singleton, unchanged>> {
    + try_start()
  }
}

package "monitor_lock" #DDEEFF {
  class MonitorLockSweeper <<runs every 30 s>>

  class MonitorLockVastSweepStrategy <<collapsed>>
  class MonitorLockModalSweepStrategy <<collapsed>>
  class MonitorLockCommunitySweepStrategy
  class MonitorLockGroupAuditSweepStrategy <<NEW>>

  MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockVastSweepStrategy
  MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockModalSweepStrategy
  MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockCommunitySweepStrategy
  MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockGroupAuditSweepStrategy
  MonitorLockVastSweepStrategy --> VastFleetMonitor
  MonitorLockModalSweepStrategy --> ModalFleetMonitor
  MonitorLockCommunitySweepStrategy --> CommunityMonitor
}

note bottom of MonitorLockVastSweepStrategy
  sweep() => vast_fleet_monitor.try_start()
  All four sweep strategies now share the
  same shape — same as community today.
end note

note bottom of MonitorLockGroupAuditSweepStrategy
  sweep() iterates active render_groups,
  calls lifecycle.reconcile_group_status(gid).
  Closes group-status drift bug class:
  chunks done but render_groups.status stuck.
end note

note as MEM #CCFFCC
  **Memory under any load (active job count irrelevant):**
   • 1 × VastFleetMonitor      = ~10 MB
   • 1 × ModalFleetMonitor     = ~10 MB
   • 1 × CommunityMonitor      = ~10 MB
   • MonitorLockSweeper        = shared (~5 MB)
   • **Total: ~35 MB**
   Down from ~1010 MB at 50+50 active jobs.
   Constant in active job count.  OOM as a class of failure: gone.
end note

note as DEL #FFE4B5
  **Deleted:**
   • vast/monitor/vast_instance_monitor.py
   • vast/monitor/vast_monitor_manager.py
   • modal/monitor/modal_job_monitor.py
   • modal/monitor/modal_monitor_manager.py
   • MonitorLockRepository.per_job_key()  (unused)
end note

@enduml
